    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-18T09:20:43+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T09:20:43+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T22:50:43Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-17T22:50:43Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of the Bight, extends a ridge of high pressure over most of South Australia. The high and ridge will move slowly eastwards during the week to be in the Tasman Sea on Thursday. A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia will move over South Australia mid to late in the week. Another high pressure system follows and moves over South Australia on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny day. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Leigh Creek at night. Winds east to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon and evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 33 to 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Leigh Creek. Winds northeast to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h in the early morning. Overnight temperatures falling to 20 to 27 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower east of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far northeast. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day then tending northwest to northeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 34 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
